# Compat lane PR-2 gate registration (follow-up spotted during PR-5): tests/test_compat_finding_event.py
# guarded the recorder's invariants but was never registered here, so it only ran by hand. One gate per
# file (246-249 are the lane's other gates). GATE-HYGIENE: description strings must contain NO dollar-sign
# and NO backtick.
register_gate "tests/test_compat_finding_event.py" "COMPAT FINDING EVENT GATE: PASS" "compat finding recorder: append-only event kind, deterministic dedupe, loud refusals, tenant walls" "compat finding recorder (compatibility lane PR-2): core.record_compat_finding_with_authority appends the content-free compat_finding event kind — producer/consumer head SHAs, a bounded fact fingerprint, and a bounded safe-charset reason code, never source text. Proven on a real database: record/read-back through the owner-pinned read; a deterministic EV-COMPAT event id makes the same (account, repo, head pair, fingerprint) idempotent while either head moving mints a new row; malformed SHAs/fingerprints/reason codes are refused loudly (ERRCODE 23514) rather than truncated, so no code-body prefix can persist; a tenant role cannot read another tenant findings row and a direct tenant INSERT naming the new columns is refused at the grant barrier; the erasure wall silences writes for an erased account." "compat finding recorder: idempotent dedupe by head pair + fingerprint, loud refusal of malformed or unsafe inputs, tenant separation and grant barrier hold, erasure wall respected. Gate 250." 20 420
